      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How many quarts is 64 oz?</h3>
        <p>64 oz = 2 quarts. A 64 oz jug holds exactly 2 quarts, which is also half a gallon (0.5 gal).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What is the difference between fluid ounces and ounces?</h3>
        <p>Fluid ounces (fl oz) measure volume — used for liquids. Regular ounces (oz) measure weight — used for solids like flour or butter. Always use fluid ounces when converting to quarts since quarts measure volume.</p>
